From 60cb73293f917c67bd5b38b73ae7ae2a14d71541 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:37:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the 5P-8P labels on Tournament Edition, in their
 characters' colours

The labels' code on TE: its sites and calls translated (srnp_game.hpp), the routine made for the game
that runs (its calls, the current texture through r13, the tags' entry and table), in free low memory
on TE (0x80002600-0x80002840: TE's first code section has no zero padding). The results' tags are left
out on TE (its names texture has another palette).

No GTSE of ours on TE: TE's decompressor refuses compresse_opt.py's stream (its own GTSE recompressed
by it crashes TE's texture loader; the original file served the same way loads), and with the game's
encoder (greedy, longest copy 2..255, nearest on ties: it gives TE's GTSE back byte for byte) the
block makes the file 2.3 KB longer than the disc's, more than the game reads from a save state. The
runner writes the mod's block (LabelsBlock: read from the srnp_etiquettes folder, left off on TE) at
the bottom of the main thread's stack (0x805E8000; the stack runs 0x805E7C40-0x8060BC40, ArenaLo,
and its lowest 110 KB stayed at zero in every TE race dumped).

TE's new characters' labels were black: the labels' colour table is the US game's 17 (TE 0x8035D7D4);
TE's HUD reads its own table of 23 (0x80372D48). The 1P labels' lookup goes there on TE (lis r3,
0x8037; slwi; addic r0, r0, 0x2D48: addi would read r0 as 0).

Measured on 2026-11-26: 8 TE runners, the labels 5P-8P on, each character's colour (Metal Sonic blue,
Blaze purple, Silver silver, Chaos light blue, Super Sonic gold), 48 identical checksums, 0 divergence;
8 US runners with the labels mod, 56 identical, 0 divergence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
